    "result": "I implemented `encode` and `decode` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub signatures, and made no other changes. `encode` scans maximal runs: runs of four or more become `~n~c`, a lone `~` becomes `~~`, and everything else is copied as is. `decode` reads left to right, treating `~~` as one `~`, and a `~` followed by a digit as a run marker. It raises `ValueError` for a trailing `~`, an invalid character after `~`, a count with a leading zero, a count below 4, a count not followed by `~`, or a missing run character. Digits are checked as ASCII `0`–`9` only. I did not run or test the code, since shell access was not available.",
